#---
# purpose: "fz-f98: Enum.reduce/2 and reduce/3 over Map do not materialize absent values"
# defer.build: one live blocker: Enum.reduce/2 over Map raises Enum.EmptyError (fz-kdt.1)
# defer.interp: one live blocker: Enum.reduce/2 over Map raises Enum.EmptyError (fz-kdt.1)
# defer.run: one live blocker: Enum.reduce/2 over Map raises Enum.EmptyError (fz-kdt.1)
#---
#
# Regression target for fz-kdt.1, re-triaged 2026-08-24: ONE bug from green.
# The reduce/3 line below is correct at HEAD (prints 3); only reduce/2 -- the
# no-accumulator form, which must take the first element as the seed -- still
# fails, and it fails as `Enum.EmptyError` rather than by dropping value
# evidence. Elixir yields `{3, :one}`.
fn main() do
  map = %{2 => :two, 1 => :one}

  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, fn ({k, _v}, {ak, av}) -> {ak + k, av} end))
  dbg(Enum.reduce(map, 0, fn ({k, _v}, acc) -> acc + k end))
end
